If you've passed the quest, then your level doesn't matter anymore.  I
would suggest finding a way to lower your level.  When you lose
levels, you'll lose those skill slots.  When you re-gain the levels,
you can re-pick the skill slots.  One caveat is that you'll lose
skills in reverse order of what you picked, so if you want to gain
enough skill slots for saber and two-weaponing (or long sword too),
make sure you've lost all the levels you need before you raise any of
them.

I'd say the best way to do this is to dance with a vampire until
eventually a level drain attack succeeds.  You can strip armor as
needed (or as you feel comfortable doing) to make this attack more
likely.  Then, just go fight some monsters or use whatever method you
want to gain the levels back and pick the right skill slots this time.

